---

<section id="artifacts" class="page-shell section-pad scroll-mt-20 border-t border-[var(--line)]">
  <h2 class="text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-[var(--text)]">Artifact sets, at a glance</h2>
  <p class="mt-3 max-w-[65ch] text-[var(--muted)]">
    The set you farm decides your damage ceiling. Here is every meta 4-piece set, what it does, and who it is for —
    pick the set that matches the reaction your team actually triggers.
  </p>

  <div class="mt-8 grid grid-cols-1 gap-4 md:grid-cols-2">
    {sets.map((s) => (
      <div class="panel p-5">
        <h3 class="font-semibold text-[var(--text)]">{s.name}</h3>
        <p class="mt-1.5 text-sm text-forest-600/90">{s.bonus}</p>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-[var(--muted)]">
          <span class="font-medium text-[var(--text)]">Best for:</span> {s.bestFor}
        </p>
        <p class="mt-1 text-xs text-[var(--muted)]/80">{s.tip}</p>
      </div>
    ))}
  </div>

  <p class="mt-6 max-w-[65ch] text-sm text-[var(--muted)]">
    A common mistake is farming a set that does not match your team’s reaction — e.g. building Crit on a Bloom trigger
    or using Gilded Dreams on a Freeze carry. Identify which reaction your team triggers, then farm the set above that
    feeds it.
  </p>
</section>
